<title>BELGIUM: Latest EU sugar data expected Wednesday.</title>
<headline>Latest EU sugar data expected Wednesday.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The latest European Union sugar production forecast for 1996/97 is expected to be released to the sugar management committee on Wednesday, an EU member state official said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Little change is expected in the European Commission's estimates,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The Commission has not yet produced a final balance sheet for 1995/96 but has said it will do so soon, the official added.</p>
<p>The last balance sheet estimate for 1996/97, released in March, put EU beet sugar output at 16.52 million tonnes, compared with the 16.34 million forecast in February and 15.56 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>The Commission also raised its forecast of &quot;C&quot;, non-quota, sugar exports to 2.44 million tonnes in 1996/97 from a previous forecast of 2.28 million.</p>
<p>The &quot;C&quot; sugar carry-over into 1996/97 totalled 685,000 tonnes while &quot;C&quot; sugar exports in 1995/96 amounted to 1.58 million tonnes.</p>
<p>&quot;Higher &quot;C&quot; sugar exports are due to increased production after an unexpectedly big crop,&quot; a Commission official said.</p>
<p>--Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
